# Sevalla parses `_headers` like `_redirects`; authored in `public/` so
# `next build` copies it to `out/_headers`.
#
# RFC 8288 Link headers advertising the machine-readable surfaces of the site
# to agents that read response headers and never parse the HTML. One line with
# comma-separated link-values (RFC 8288 section 3), not repeated `Link:` lines:
# `_headers` merges matching rules by header name, and repeated names are not
# guaranteed to survive that merge.
#
# A page's Markdown sibling is not advertised here — `_headers` does not
# interpolate `:placeholder` captures into header values, so a site-wide rule
# could only point at one fixed `.md` file. Markdown is reached through
# `Accept: text/markdown` negotiation instead (see `_redirects`).
/*
  Link: </sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"; type="application/xml", </llms.txt>; rel="llms-txt"; type="text/plain", </llms-full.txt>; rel="llms-txt-full"; type="text/plain"
